From: Johan Alvarado <contact@c127.dev>
Date: Thu, 11 Sep 2026 18:44:14 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 2/2] spi: spi-qpic-snand: drop the redundant ECC context
 handling

With the context published where it is created, the scratch qpic_ecc allocated
in qcom_spi_probe() and the assignment in
qcom_spi_ecc_prepare_io_req_pipelined() are both dead: the first only ever
existed to give the ooblayout callbacks something non-NULL to read, and the
second re-published on every page I/O what init_ctx now publishes once.

No functional change when applied after the context-publication fix. It is not
independent of it: applied alone to an unfixed baseline this would remove the
pointer initialisation without supplying the replacement.

[Backport note, not part of the upstream submission: upstream commit
 8d6911645478, applied by Mark Brown to broonie/spi.git for-7.4 on 2026-09-18,
 as 2/2 of the series whose first patch is carried here as 0955. Same caveat on
 the hash. Split from 0955 so that either can be removed once the kernel here
 supplies the corresponding change - if it gains only the functional fix, drop
 0955 and keep this; it does NOT mean either may be omitted on its own.]

[The explanation above is LOCAL commentary, rewritten here - it is not the
 upstream author's commit message reproduced verbatim, and should not be read as
 his words. Only the code change is his.

 No Signed-off-by from the author either: the upstream commit certainly carries
 one, but it has not been read from here and inventing another person's DCO
 certification is not an option. Mine is added as the person carrying it, which
 is the part I can certify; recover and restore his trailer before this is ever
 passed on anywhere that matters.]

Signed-off-by: Muhammad Huda Nugroho <mhudan21@gmail.com>
---
--- a/drivers/spi/spi-qpic-snand.c
+++ b/drivers/spi/spi-qpic-snand.c
@@ -431,9 +431,7 @@
 						 struct nand_page_io_req *req)
 {
 	struct qcom_nand_controller *snandc = nand_to_qcom_snand(nand);
-	struct qpic_ecc *ecc_cfg = nand_to_ecc_ctx(nand);
 
-	snandc->qspi->ecc = ecc_cfg;
 	snandc->qspi->raw_rw = false;
 	snandc->qspi->oob_rw = false;
 	snandc->qspi->page_rw = false;
@@ -1539,15 +1537,10 @@
 	struct spi_controller *ctlr;
 	struct qcom_nand_controller *snandc;
 	struct qpic_spi_nand *qspi;
-	struct qpic_ecc *ecc;
 	struct resource *res;
 	const void *dev_data;
 	int ret;
 
-	ecc = devm_kzalloc(dev, sizeof(*ecc), GFP_KERNEL);
-	if (!ecc)
-		return -ENOMEM;
-
 	qspi = devm_kzalloc(dev, sizeof(*qspi), GFP_KERNEL);
 	if (!qspi)
 		return -ENOMEM;
@@ -1564,7 +1557,6 @@
 	snandc->dev = dev;
 	snandc->qspi = qspi;
 	snandc->qspi->ctlr = ctlr;
-	snandc->qspi->ecc = ecc;
 
 	dev_data = of_device_get_match_data(dev);
 	if (!dev_data) {
